```

`data-theme="light"` is on the server-rendered `<html>` so the document is never attribute-less; the script overwrites it before paint when the resolved theme is dark. `suppressHydrationWarning` covers both the `js` class and the `data-theme` rewrite.

`Grain` is the last child of `<body>` — DOM order plus `z-index: 9999` puts it above everything without any other element needing a z-index at all.

`<main>` carries `tabIndex={-1}` so the skip link and route-change focus can move focus into it programmatically, and `outline-none` because a programmatic focus on a landmark should not draw a ring (the ring belongs to `:focus-visible` on interactive elements). Removing the outline on a non-interactive, programmatically-focused container is the one sanctioned case; every interactive element keeps its ring from the 2.1 base layer.

### 4. Skip link

First focusable element in the document, positioned off-screen until focused. It is a real link with a real target, not a visually hidden decoration.

```tsx
